SUMMARY:Deadline 10:00 GMT: n-Space Fellowship\, Singapore Fellow (Predicti
 on): 9-month art and technology fellowship with 3 months at Somerset House
  Studios\, London (GBP 5\,000 fee\, travel and accommodation covered)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 07 Dec 2026 at 10:00 GMT.\n\nThe Singapore place in the 
 second n-Space fellowship cohort at Somerset House Studios\, run with the 
 National Arts Council Singapore. n-Space is a space for experimental\, col
 laborative research across art\, technology and society\; this cohort of s
 ix (five London-based fellows plus the Singapore fellow) is convened aroun
 d PREDICTION as a line of enquiry\, from forecasting and sensing infrastru
 ctures...\n\nOrganisation: Somerset House Studios with the National Arts C
 ouncil Singapore\; research partner UAL Creative Computing Institute\; sup
 ported by the Rothschild Foundation\nLocation: Hybrid. In person at Somers
 et House Studios\, London\, UK from April to June 2027 and for the final p
 resentation in March 2028\; online from July 2027 to February 2028. Open t
 o Singapore citizens and permanent residents.\nAward: GBP 5\,000 fellowshi
 p fee\, plus return flights to London\, accommodation\, per diems and grou
 nd transport for both London visits\, and access to a GBP 30\,000 R&D fund
  shared by the six-person cohort. No application fee mentioned.\nDuration:
  9 months\, April 2027 to March 2028 (April to June 2027 in residence in L
 ondon)\n\nMore: https://www.somersethouse.org.uk/somerset-house-studios/re
 sidencies-and-opportunities/n-space-fellowship-open-call-singapore-fellow?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.somersethouse.org.uk/somerset-house-studios/residencies-and
 -opportunities/n-space-fellowship-open-call-singapore-fellow?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hybrid. In person at Somerset House Studios\, London\, UK from Apr
 il to June 2027 and for the final presentation in March 2028\; online from
  July 2027 to February 2028. Open to Singapore citizens and permanent resi
 dents.
